First experiment: halve the global batch from 524,288 to 262,144 tokens while keeping the GPU microbatch unchanged. This removes gradient accumulation, roughly doubles optimizer-update frequency at nearly the same token throughput, and should improve sample efficiency within the fixed wall-clock budget.

