codex
Muon is a strong keep: `val_bpb` fell to **1.089922**, despite processing only 175.7M tokens. Its current implementation orthogonalizes each matrix in a separate call, which costs about 21% throughput. Next I’m batching same-shaped matrices into three-dimensional tensors so Newton–Schulz runs a few batched kernels per step; the update math stays the same, but more of the 180 seconds should go to model tokens.
